.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt KMALLOC 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm kmalloc ,
.Nm kzalloc
.Nd allocate kernel memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In vm/vm_kmem.h
.Ft void *
.Fn kmalloc "size_t size"
.Ft void *
.Fn kzalloc "size_t size"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn kmalloc
function allocates
.Fa size
bytes of kernel memory.
The allocated memory is uninitialized.
.Pp
The
.Fn kzalloc
function allocates
.Fa size
bytes of kernel memory and initializes it to zero.
.Pp
The allocated memory must be freed with
.Fn kfree 9
when it is no longer needed.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn kmalloc
and
.Fn kzalloc
functions return a pointer to the allocated memory, or
.Dv NULL
if the allocation failed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kfree 9 ,
.Xr kmem_init 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn kmalloc
function first appeared in Substrate.
